{"name":"Upstate","hex":"#cac7b8","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"upstate","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The northern section of a state.","The inland section of a state, particularly of South Carolina."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the northern section of a state."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/upstate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Upstate California","blocks":[{"text":"Upstate California is the name of a marketing campaign which seeks to promote business in the northernmost 20 counties of California. Roughly the upper half of Northern California, the \"upstate\" designation encompasses primarily rural areas which contain 4.5% of California's population. Outside of public relations, this area is often referred to as far Northern California."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Map_of_Northern_and_Upstate_California.png/330px-Map_of_Northern_and_Upstate_California.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upstate_California","wikidata":"Q2480534"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"upstate":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-upstate.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-upstate.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-upstate.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-upstate.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-upstate.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-upstate2.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a